# 🔐 ZK Security Guide

## Overview

Zero-Knowledge systems enable proving knowledge without revealing secrets. Vulnerabilities can occur at:
- **Circuit arithmetization** - constraint design errors
- **Compilation** - incorrect transformations
- **Proof generation/verification** - cryptographic flaws
- **System integration** - boundary condition issues

Key properties at risk:
- **Soundness** - false proofs accepted
- **Completeness** - valid proofs rejected
- **Zero-Knowledge** - secret information leaked

---

## 1. Missing Range Checks

```javascript
// VULNERABLE - o1js example
// Limbs not constrained to valid range
static check(signature: EcdsaSignature) {
    // Missing range check on r, s components
    // Value could be split incorrectly: 1 + 1*2 + 1*4 == 1 + 3*2
}

// SECURE - enforce range on each limb
static check(signature: EcdsaSignature) {
    // Ensure each limb is within [0, 2^88 - 1]
    this.Curve.Scalar.assertAlmostReduced(signature.r, signature.s);
}

// Circom example - missing range check
template BadMul() {
    signal input a;
    signal input b;
    signal output c;
    c <== a * b;  // a, b could be any value in field!
}

// SECURE
template GoodMul(n) {
    signal input a;
    signal input b;
    signal output c;
    
    // Constrain inputs to n bits
    component rangeA = Num2Bits(n);
    component rangeB = Num2Bits(n);
    rangeA.in <== a;
    rangeB.in <== b;
    
    c <== a * b;
}
```

