## 2. Under-Constrained Circuits

Variables not adequately constrained can be set to any value by malicious prover.

```circom
// VULNERABLE - unused intermediate value
template BadHash() {
    signal input preimage;
    signal output hash;
    
    signal intermediate;
    intermediate <-- someComputation(preimage);  // <-- not <==
    // intermediate is UNCONSTRAINED - prover can set arbitrarily
    
    hash <== poseidon(preimage);
}

// SECURE - all signals constrained
template GoodHash() {
    signal input preimage;
    signal output hash;
    
    signal intermediate;
    intermediate <== someComputation(preimage);  // <== constrains
    
    hash <== poseidon(preimage);
}
```

### Assignment vs Constraint
```circom
// <-- is witness assignment (no constraint)
// <== is constrained assignment (adds constraint)
// === is constraint only

a <-- b;     // a gets value b, NO constraint
a <== b;     // a gets value b AND constraint: a === b
a === b;     // constraint only: a must equal b
```

