## 7. Recursive Verification Issues

```rust
// VULNERABLE - SP1 recursive verifier
// 1. committed_value_digest unconstrained if COMMIT not called
// 2. next_pc == 0 not checked on first layer

// Attack:
// 1. Abort program before COMMIT syscall
// 2. committed_value_digest defaults to zero (unconstrained)
// 3. Modify to any arbitrary value
// 4. Mark is_complete = true to bypass next_pc check
// 5. Generate "valid" proof for invalid execution

// SECURE
// 1. Always constrain committed_value_digest
// 2. Check next_pc == 0 on ALL layers of recursive tree
```

