## 8. Forging ZK Proofs

```rust
// VULNERABLE - zkWasm LoadN instruction constraints
// Load8 should zero upper 56 bits, but only checks bits 9-16
constraint_builder.push(
    "op_load pick value size check",
    vec![
        is_one_byte.expr(meta) * load_picked_leading_u16_u8_high.expr(meta),
        // Only constrains bits 9-16 to zero!
        // Bits 17-64 can be anything
    ]
);

// ATTACK:
// Memory contains: 0x1122334455667788
// Valid Load8 should return: 0x0000000000000088
// Attacker crafts: 0xAAAAAAAABBBB0088
// System accepts as valid Load8 result!

// SECURE - constrain ALL upper bits
is_one_byte.expr(meta) * (
    load_picked.u16_cells_le[1].expr(meta) +  // bits 17-32
    load_picked.u16_cells_le[2].expr(meta) +  // bits 33-48
    load_picked.u16_cells_le[3].expr(meta)    // bits 49-64
)
```

